    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1092">

                <pb facs="1020" n="762" xml:id="pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72.111R24/36</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: The Imperial Consul
                    General at San Francisco has reported to me and also informed the United States
                    attorney there that a printing office of the place has been carrying on British
                    recruiting for several months. On Wednesday morning, thirty-two men, almost all
                    Americans, were enlisted and entrained in through Tourist Car 1606 for the
                    journey to Chicago, where they arrived early to-day. Other recruits are to join
                    from Ogden and Omaha. Thence they are to proceed to New York, where, it is
                    alleged, they will be embarked by the White Star Line.</p>
                <p>I have the honor very respectfully to bring to your excellency’s knowledge the
                    above incident, which appears to me to involve a British violation of American
                    neutrality.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
